/**

@page WFS_SQ_QUERY_HANDLERS Stored query handlers


Stored query handlers are implemented as C++ classes derived from
base class SmartMet::Plugin::WFS::StoredQueryHandlerBase and optionally also
from one or more of classes implementing
@ref WFS_SQ_PARAM_GROUPS "stored query handler parameter groups".

The handler factory named by the stored query configuration entry @b constructor_name
is looked up at run time with dlsym(), so the factory objects must have external linkage
(see wfs/stored_queries/StoredQueryHandlerFactories.h).

Following stored query handlers are currently available:

- @subpage WFS_SQ_GET_FEATURE_BY_ID "GetFeatureByID handler"
- @subpage WFS_SQ_DATA_SET_BY_ID "GetDataSetByID handler"
- @subpage WFS_SQ_GENERIC_OBS "Observation data queries handler"
- @subpage WFS_SQ_FLASH_OBS_HANDLER "Lightning observation data query handler"
- @subpage WFS_SQ_FORECAST_QUERY_HANDLER "Forecast data query handler"
- @subpage WFS_SQ_QE_DOWNLOAD_HANDLER "QEngine data download query handler"
- @subpage WFS_SQ_GEOSERVER_DOWNLOAD_HANDLER "GeoServer data download handler"
- @subpage WFS_SQ_FILE_QUERY_HANDLER "File download handler"
- @subpage WFS_SQ_AVIATION_OBSERVATION_QUERY_HANDLER "Aviation observations handler"
- @subpage WFS_SQ_MAST_QUERY_HANDLER "Mast profile observation handler"
- @subpage WFS_SQ_AIR_NUCLIDE_QUERY_HANDLER "Air Radionuclide activity concentration data handler"
- @subpage WFS_SQ_GRID_FORECAST_QUERY_HANDLER "Grid engine forecast data query handler"
- @subpage WFS_SQ_ENV_MONITORING_NETWORK_QUERY_HANDLER "Environmental monitoring network handler"
- @subpage WFS_SQ_ENV_MONITORING_FACILITY_QUERY_HANDLER "Environmental monitoring facility handler"

*/